.TH HD-THEME 7 "October 2026" "hd-desktop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-theme \- the theme engine of HyprDebian
.SH DESCRIPTION
The themes are JSON files in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/themes ,
one per theme, named
.IR <name>.json .
A theme that is selected is copied, with its name, to the key
.B hd-theme
of a configuration, see
.BR hd-config (7).
There are two:
.TP
the theme of the system
in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
selected by root.
It is the theme of the system itself, of the boot splash of
.BR hd-plymouth (7),
of the graphical bootloader of
.BR hd-bootloader (7),
of new users and of every user who has no theme of their own.
.TP
the theme of a user
in
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json ,
selected by that user.
.PP
Programs of the desktop, such as
.BR hd-menu (1),
read the theme of the user who runs them: the key
.B hd-theme
of
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
when it is there, else that of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
else defaults of their own.
Root uses the theme of the system.
.PP
.BR hd-theme (1)
adds, deletes, lists and selects themes, and with
.B \-\-apply
writes the theme files of the desktop programs in the home directory of a
user from the theme of that user; each user runs that after a theme is selected.
.BR hd-theme-card (1)
renders a theme into a card, a PNG that shows it.
.SH THEMES
A theme is a JSON object with all of these members, and no others:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
    "font": "JetBrainsMono NFM Medium",
    "font-size-big": 24,
    "font-size-normal": 18,
    "font-size-small": 14,
    "highlight": "#ff6600",
    "normal": "#0066cc",
    "dark": "#071422",
    "light": "#e6edf5",
    "border": 4,
    "radius": 10,
    "gap": 4,
    "opacity": 0.8,
    "icon_size": 48,
    "background": "emerald"
}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B font
The font of all text, a fontconfig family and style of a monospaced font.
.TP
.BR font-size-big ", " font-size-normal ", " font-size-small
The sizes of text, in points: banners and input fields, menus and
notifications, terminals and small labels.
.TP
.B dark
The background of bars, menus and windows, drawn at
.BR opacity .
.TP
.B normal
The background of the selected item, unfocused borders and dividers.
.TP
.B highlight
Focus only: the outline of the focused window, menu or input field.
Never a fill behind text.
.TP
.B light
All text, also on
.BR normal .
.TP
.B border
The width of borders, in pixels.
.TP
.B radius
The outer radius of the corners of windows and menus, in pixels, at least
.BR border .
Anything inside a border has the inner radius,
.B radius
minus
.BR border .
.TP
.B gap
The distance between windows, in pixels.
.TP
.B opacity
The opacity of
.BR dark ,
from 0 to 1.
Text and borders stay opaque, except in VSCodium and Obsidian, which have no
background opacity of their own: Hyprland draws their whole window at
.BR opacity .
.TP
.B icon_size
The size of icons, in pixels.
.TP
.B background
A family of images in
.IR /usr/share/backgrounds/hyprdebian ,
named
.IR <family>-<width>x<height>.png .
A screen shows the smallest one that covers it, else the largest.
.PP
In
.IR config.json ,
the key
.B hd-theme
also has the member
.BR name ,
the name of the theme.
.SH SCALING
The sizes of a theme are made for a screen of 96 pixels per inch seen from
70 cm.
The key
.B hd-display
of the configuration of the system,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
tells how the monitor of the machine differs from that, so the theme looks
the same size on every machine.
Root sets it with
.BR hd-config-update (1),
in one of two ways:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"diagonal": 42, "distance": 90}
{"factor": 1.4}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR diagonal ", " distance
The diagonal of the monitor in inches, and the distance from which it is
seen, in centimetres.
The factor is
.IP
.RS
.nf
dpi = sqrt(width\(S2 + height\(S2) / diagonal
factor = dpi / 96 \(mu distance / 70
.fi
.RE
.IP
to two decimals, with the width and the height in pixels of the preferred
mode of the connected monitor with the most pixels, in
.IR /sys/class/drm .
The diagonal is given, not read from the monitor, as monitors often report
a wrong size.
.TP
.B factor
The factor itself.
It wins over a diagonal and a distance.
.PP
The font sizes,
.BR border ,
.BR radius ,
.B gap
and
.B icon_size
are multiplied by the factor: by
.B hd-theme \-\-apply
in the theme files, see
.BR hd-theme (1),
by
.BR hd-menu (1)
and
.BR hd-message (1)
when they start, and by
.BR hd-launcher-cache (1)
for the icons of the launcher.
The font sizes are rounded to a tenth of a point, the others to whole
pixels, and a size that is not 0 stays at least 1.
The themes and the key
.B hd-theme
keep their own sizes.
Without the key, or when it is not valid, which is reported, the factor
is 1.
.PP
The theme is scaled in the place of Hyprland, so all stays sharp, on whole
pixels: the monitor rule in the
.I hyprland.lua
that new users get has scale 1.
A scale above 1 would scale the theme twice.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/themes/<name>.json
The themes.
The themes
.IR default ,
on the wallpaper emerald,
.IR sand ,
in browns on lines\-sand, and
.IR mulberry ,
in reds and purples on softwaves\-mulberry and in SauceCodePro NFM Medium,
come with hd-desktop.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The key
.B hd-theme
holds the theme of the system, the key
.B hd-display
the scale of the theme on the monitor.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/hd-desktop/hd_display.py
Works out the factor of
.B hd-display
for
.B hd-theme
and
.BR hd-launcher-cache .
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
The key
.B hd-theme
holds the theme of the user, when they selected one.
.TP
.I /var/cache/hd-theme/cards/<name>.png
The cards of the themes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-theme (1),
.BR hd-theme-card (1),
.BR hd-config (7),
.BR hd-menu (1),
.BR hd-message (1),
.BR hd-plymouth (7)
